package UI

// A view is a UI<M>: an immutable tree whose buttons and inputs send values
// of the app's message enum M (README "Typed views"). Bare UI in a function's
// signature takes the message type of its arguments.
//
// The widgets that send messages are compiler-owned: they are generic over
// the message enum, which an ordinary Oct function cannot be. They are
// reached through the UI namespace and can be written as markup tags:
//
//     UI.Button(label: String, on: M, enabled: Bool) -> UI<M>
//     UI.Checkbox(label: String, checked: Bool, on: fn(Bool) -> M) -> UI<M>
//     UI.TextField(value: String, on: fn(String) -> M) -> UI<M>
//     UI.Slider(value: Float, min: Float, max: Float, on: fn(Float) -> M) -> UI<M>
//
// Inputs are controlled: the model owns the value, and the input proposes a
// change by calling `on`, which builds the message Update receives. A
// payload variant is such a function: UI.Checkbox("Audio", model.Audio,
// Msg.SetAudio). The session owns only transient state (hover, press,
// focus, caret), keyed by node identity.

// The canonical text form of a view: node kinds, ids, specs and messages.
// Tests compare views by it.
fn Signature(node: UI) -> String {
    return UISignature(node)
}
